    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0387" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg259"/>

                <head>No. 198.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram<anchor n="*" xml:id="d198-f1"
                    />.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>. [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-27">undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Becerra</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colombian Minister, Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Yesterday afternoon Aizpurú arranged with the American admiral that the latter’s
                    forces should retire to the railway station, those of Aizpurú to maintain order
                    in the city until the arrival of the expedition from Cauca (Buenaventura), when
                    they will go out of the city with full liberty to give battle in the open
                    country.</p>
                <p>Between 7 and 8 at night the Americans retired.</p>
                <closer><signed>TELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d198-f1" n="*" xml:id="d198-f1-content">
                <p>Shown to Mr. Bayard by Mr. Becerra, April 27.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
